crosspost-design
=================

An adaptation of **gzh-design-skill** — https://github.com/isjiamu/gzh-design-skill
Copyright (C) 2026 甲木 (Jiamu) × 摸鱼小李 (Moyu Xiaoli), AGPL-3.0.

The upstream project formats Markdown for WeChat Official Accounts (公众号) in
Chinese. This project targets Telegram Instant View, VK, Dzen and Habr in
English and Russian. It is a derivative work and stays under AGPL-3.0.

What was kept
-------------
* The overall skill shape: `SKILL.md` as the workflow, `references/` as the
  library of record, `scripts/` as deterministic gates, `assets/` for samples,
  `references/eval-cases.md` for regression cases.
* The editorial philosophy: recipes per article type, a hierarchy budget, a
  single source of truth for platform facts, "never hand-write the output".
* The two-gate quality loop: a design linter before the build, a compliance
  validator after it.

What was adapted from upstream code
-----------------------------------
* `scripts/extract_docx.py` — ported from the upstream extractor; Chinese style
  names replaced with English/Russian/German/French heading styles, italics
  added, messages translated.
* `scripts/wrap_preview.py` and `assets/preview-template.html` — the copy-to-
  clipboard preview idea and DOM-selection technique come from upstream; the
  page was rewritten for EN/RU, dark mode and multiple target editors.

What was replaced entirely
--------------------------
* **Themes → platform profiles.** Upstream carries six colour themes of inline
  CSS because WeChat allows arbitrary inline styles. None of the four targets
  here allow any CSS, so colour themes are meaningless. Their role is taken by
  `references/platform-*.md` (markup whitelists) and
  `references/structure-recipes.md` (skeleton and voice).
* **Full-width CJK punctuation → EN/RU micro-typography.**
  `scripts/typography_lint.py` replaces the 全角 checks with «ёлочки», curly
  quotes, em/en dashes, ellipses and non-breaking spaces, with `--fix`.
* **`validate_gzh_html.py` → `scripts/validate_post.py`**, a per-platform
  whitelist checker (telegra.ph nodes, Bot API HTML, VK paste, Dzen
  content:encoded, Habr Flavored Markdown).
* **`component_lint.py` → `scripts/source_lint.py`**, which lints the canonical
  source for design failures instead of linting theme libraries.
* **New: `scripts/build_targets.py`** — the canonical-Markdown parser and the
  five renderers. Nothing equivalent exists upstream, where the model assembles
  HTML from component libraries by hand.
* **New: `scripts/telegraph_publish.py`** — publishes the built body to
  telegra.ph, which gives Instant View without writing a template.

Platform facts in `references/` were verified against, and are cited from:
telegra.ph/api, instantview.telegram.org/docs, core.telegram.org/bots/api,
habr.com/ru/docs/help/markdown/, habr.com/ru/docs/help/wysiwyg/ and
dzen.ru/help/ru/website/rss-modify.html. Re-verify before trusting them after
any platform update.
